      "text": "A bicycle operates through a sophisticated mechanical system that converts human muscular energy into forward motion via a chain-driven transmission. When the rider pedals, their legs exert force on the crank arms, which rotate the chainring; this rotation pulls the chain, transferring torque to the rear sprocket and subsequently to the rear wheel, causing it to spin against the ground. The friction between the tire and the road surface generates traction, propelling the bicycle forward, while the rider maintains balance and direction through the steering mechanism, which allows the front wheel to pivot for maneuvering. Simultaneously, the bicycle\u2019s structural integrity relies on a rigid frame that supports the rider\u2019s weight and distributes forces evenly, while the wheels, equipped with bearings, minimize rotational resistance, ensuring efficient energy transfer from the pedals to the ground.<|im_end|>",
